From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elena Maher <12779416+elenaOnline@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 06:21:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gpui: Pass an input method's clause underlines with its
 marked text

A composition in an input method (Japanese, Chinese, Korean) is shown in
clauses: every text view underlines each clause, thick under the one being
converted and thin under the others, so the user sees which part the next
conversion applies to. GPUI's macOS view took only the marked text's
string and said it read no marked text attributes, so a GPUI text input
could only draw one underline under all of it.

The view now asks for the underline and clause attributes
(`validAttributesForMarkedText`) and reads the underlines as browsers do:
one per run of `NSUnderlineStyleAttributeName`, thick when the style is
above single, in the run's `NSUnderlineColorAttributeName` if it has one.
An attribute value of another type than the attribute's (a style that is
no number, a colour that is no `NSColor`) is left alone: a message it does
not answer would raise an Objective-C exception, which cannot unwind out
of the view's `setMarkedText:` and would abort. The underlines reach the
input handler as `MarkedTextUnderline`s through
`InputHandler::replace_and_mark_text_with_underlines` (and the same on
`EntityInputHandler`), whose default ignores them and calls
`replace_and_mark_text_in_range`, so existing handlers are unchanged.
`gpui_macos::marked_text_underlines` is public for text views that read
attributed marked text themselves (and for tests).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
